A||||17||pHoOl||Value of 88 coupe||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||05-20-2001||12:34 AM||||Alrighty, i have a question for you all.  <P>I'm thinking of looking at a fiero tomorrow which is an 88 with T-tops and 5sp.  it has 8X,000 miles, and the ad didn't say if it was coupe, GT or Formula.  The guy is asking 3500 for it i believe.  (all of this was relayed to me by my dad)<P>So... here is the question.  What would it be worth if it were a coupe, GT, or formula.  I'm trying to get a feel for it, because if it ends up making sense, i might sell my GT for it.  I'm thinkin that if it is a coupe, it would not be anywhere near worth 3500, even if it was in good condition.  <P>What do you guys think?  Personally, i've been itchin for a stick, and t-tops are definately nice.  Also, how slow is the 4 banger.  I mean, i don't jet around with the v6, but i'd like to be able to have some acceleration so that i dont' get killed on the highway pulling out in front of someone.<P>thanks for input!!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sjp777||05-20-2001||12:55 AM||||An 88GT or Formula with T-tops and that mileage is probably worth around $6k if it's in good shape. Deduct $3k if it's a 4 cyl.<P>The difference between the coupes and the GTs/Formulas is more than just the motor and cosmetics. The Coupes did not have the WS6 suspension.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><P><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||05-20-2001||01:55 AM||||I have two 88 coupes... one T-top, one sunroof... both have plenty enough power to keep from getting killed. Not like a V6, and not even like my 4-speed Indy, but still plenty. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-20-2001||07:48 AM||||spj777, Not exactly true. All Formulas had WS6 supensions, Coupes did not have it as part of the package could be ordered with it. I have one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||05-20-2001||08:45 AM||||That was going to be another question was if it had the ws6 suspension.  I guess that there is just something that i like about taking turns and not having the car lean at all.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||05-20-2001||08:54 AM||||Just check the RPO codes on the top of the drivers side inner fender. There is a fair chance even a coupe may have it if it was special ordered. Better suspension was an easy sell.||||reg||1
Z||000006||spideyfoot||05-20-2001||10:11 AM||||My 88 coupe does not seem to lean. I would drive it first, You know t tops and good gas mileage arent such a bad thing either. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Master_Sushi||05-20-2001||10:39 AM||||I think an 88 coupe with t-tops and 5 speed would be worth a fair amount. Not as much as a V6 but still at least 4000 if its in perfect shape and 88k miles. If I could have any fiero it would be an 88 coupe t-top, 5 speed with all the options including ws6. Also my 88coupe dosent lean much, if any in corners and its non-ws6 :P.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Songman||05-20-2001||11:31 AM||||My 88 t-top coupe is automatic and it don't bother me a bit. As far as the suspension, I don't know what it is, but it is worn out. It sits pretty good and doesn't seem to be sagging on any corners but any size bump at all and the driver's side rear bottoms out. Wonder if WS6 can be bolted on. Wonder what it would cost? And also are there aftermarket alternatives that would give more bang for the buck? This is my car tp modify so I'm not worried about stock.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||pHoOl||05-21-2001||12:07 AM||||I'm tryin to figure out what it is that i like about the GT.  Cause i really don't open it up that much.  I do like the body stying though.  But then again, i'm sure that the coupe style would grow on me if i ended up tradeing.  ahh well, should be a fun time lookign at it.<P>Anybody have 0-60 times for the coupe?  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||05-21-2001||08:19 AM||||Hey Songman, get some WS6 rear springs and your problem will be solved forever.  When I bought my 88 Coupe, the rear springs were shot (at 66K miles!).  It had a bad case of drag-a$$ and the rear tires were cambered in so badly that the outer edge of the rear tires still had tread while the inner edge was worn to the cord.  It would bottom over any bump.<P>Got some springs off a wrecked Formula from the Fiero Store and now my rear end stays up where it belongs.||||reg||10
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||05-21-2001||02:40 PM||||I have an auto duke, I can get 0-60 in about 9-10 secs, maybe less on a perfect run. I’m sure a 5 speed is a few secs faster. I’m guessing like mid 8s. I have a few rough sound of my duke. Heres the link...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/master_sushi2000/sounds.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/master_sushi2000/sounds.html</A> <P>The recordings aren’t that great, but still gives you an idea.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000012||Songman||05-21-2001||07:07 PM||||Hey Chad or anyone else that knows..<BR>Is the WS6 a rear only or a front and rear setup. About what should I expect to pay for a used full WS6?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Master_Sushi||05-22-2001||12:13 AM||||Im not 100% sure, but wasnt the 88 WS6 just stiffer springs and a rear sway bar? Also, ive heard its not possable to install a rear swaybar on an auto fiero without droping the engine.<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000014||pHoOl||05-22-2001||12:16 AM||||Shoot, what did you do to your duke to make it so fast?  i don't get times like that in my auto GT<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||05-22-2001||08:40 AM||||According to everything I've been able to dig up (and it's not much), the 1988 WS6 suspension had firmer front AND rear springs and a rear sway bar.  The Y99 suspension (Coupe only) had softer springs and no rear sway bar.  <P>I've heard the WS6 had firmer suspension bushings, but have found no evidence to back that up so take that with a grain of salt.<P>All I know is, my car stopped sagging in the back and seems to understeer less with the WS6 rear springs than it did before (still has Y99 up front).  I changed shocks at the same time, though, so that's not really scientific.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChadMan||05-22-2001||09:51 AM||||Duh...I guess I only answered 1/2 your question.  I paid $50 for my rear springs from the Fiero Store (used)...I'm guessing fronts would be comparable.  The '88 sway bars are much harder to come by and I have never heard of one selling for less than $100.  Looks like they'd be much harder to install than the '84-'87, too.<P>Hey Master_Sushi, those .mp3 files sound pretty cool.  My Duke doesn't sound that cool.  And the only way mine would make it to 60 in 8 seconds is if one of you 3.4 or 3800 guys pushed me!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Master_Sushi||05-22-2001||12:24 PM||||Ya, I'd never be able to hit 8 secs without a 5 speed or some performance stuff. 9-10 is my best right now. Ive never driven a stick shift fiero, so Im just guessing about the 8 secs with a 5 speed and good clutch. I dono about the sound  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, my cars almost all orignal right now, I know my muffler is probably going so maybe thats why it sounds  bit louder <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">. Those sounds were taken with a micro recorder siting in the passanger seat with the windows up. But it is a low mileage 2.5 and car (55k), so its still at the prime of its life. Im going to get a performance dual exhaust and some modest performance add ons some time, ill take new sounds when i get those in.||||reg||1
